# ============================================================
# EIBO — repository scope
# Tracked:     knowledge files, scripts, src/, docs/, tests/, artifacts/ (evidence)
# Excluded:    runtime logs, caches, bulk data, credentials
# Rationale:   the project's entire evidentiary chain is "every reported number
#              maps to an artifact's bytes", so artifacts/ MUST be tracked.
# ============================================================

# --- Runtime output that is NOT evidence ---
# logs/ also contains logs/chats/ (conversation transcripts) -> never publish.
logs/
checkpoints/
data_snapshots/
study-packages/

# --- Tooling / environment state ---
.agent-ml/
.claude/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc

# --- Bulk data and weights: never track (corpora, checkpoints) ---
# ANCHORED to the repository root. A BARE `data/` matches at ANY depth, so it also
# excluded artifacts/**/data/ -- i.e. the evidence chain itself, which is the one
# thing this repository exists to preserve. Bulk kinds are excluded by extension.
/data/
# The evidence chain is NEVER excluded, whatever a directory is called. Placed
# before the extension rules so those still win for genuinely bulky kinds.
!artifacts/**/data/
!artifacts/**/data/**
*.h5
*.pcap
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.pkl

# --- Bulk intermediates inside artifacts that are regenerable, not cited ---
artifacts/tmp/
artifacts/*.tmp

# --- Server-only payloads: too large to track, named in README.md ------------
# These MUST come after the !artifacts/**/data/** negation above, or that
# negation re-includes them and ~3.4 GB enters the repository. k=5 wrote three
# ~1.14 GB score payloads (per_class_scores__{lightgbm,prototype,ronetc}.npz);
# they are load-bearing (per-flow error is reconstructable from them) but they
# stay on the server, and README.md lists them by name as the exception to the
# byte-traceability claim.
*.npz
# --- Stale scaffolding from an earlier repo attempt (referenced by no script) ---
.eibo_remote_gitignore
.work/


# --- LaTeX build byproducts (docs/paper/) --------------------------------
# Regenerable from the .tex sources; tracking them would put churn between a
# reader and the source. The compiled main.pdf IS tracked deliberately -- it is
# the deliverable that gets reviewed. Negation comes after the byproduct rules
# so it wins for that one file.
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
!docs/paper/main.pdf

# --- Transient tool state (regenerated per run; the .lock siblings are tracked) ---
_paper_audit_state.json
_verify_refs_state.json
.agentic-figure/

# --- Figure build scratch (candidate renders, not deliverables) ---
artifacts/_project/chart/_scratch/
